摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Bidirectional bridge between Hermes Agent and DeepSeek Harness (DSH). v0.2.4 — single-bundle Cordis plugin replacing the archived hermes-foundation/-oneshot-arbitrate/-dispatch-bridge triad.","id":"gh:1343938722","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-hermes-link","slug":"Tianbuyu-wwx/dsh-hermes-link","topics":["cordis","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-bundle","dsh-plugin","hermes","hermes-link","session-sync"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Bidirectional bridge between Hermes Agent and DeepSeek Harness (DSH). v0.2.4 — single-bundle Cordis "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"plugin replacing the archived hermes-foundation/-oneshot-arbitrate/-dispatch-bridge triad."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-hermes-link"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"> Bidirectional bridge between **Hermes Agent** and **DeepSeek Harness (DSH)**. Hermes dispatches fo"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"cused tasks (one-shot or continuable) via JSON-RPC over `POST /mcp/collab`; DSH spawns sub-agents, r"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"eturns real measured tokens, and lets you **continue any Hermes session as a native DSH session in t"},{"id":"p3s4","text":"easured tokens, and lets you **continue any Hermes session as a native DSH session in the sidebar**."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"## Why dsh-hermes-link exists"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Hermes is an *agent*-*orch-estrator* — it plans the work, picks the skill, loads the knowledge slice"},{"id":"p5s2","text":". DSH is a *coding-runtime* — it runs sub-agents, edits files, runs shells, talks to LLMs. Each tool"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" does its job well in isolation; the question was always how to make them *one system* without dragg"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"ing each one's concerns into the other."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Earlier we ran this as three separate plugins (`hermes-foundation`, `hermes-oneshot-arbitrate`, `her"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"mes-dispatch-bridge`). That triad is now archived under `dsh-hermes` with an `archive/hermes-legacy-"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"2026-08-22` tag — `dsh-hermes-link` is the single plugin that replaced them, and this repository is "},{"id":"p6s4","text":"the home of that replacement."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"### Agent-communication line (Hermes → DSH)"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"- **`POST /mcp/collab`** — JSON-RPC 2.0 endpoint Hermes posts to.\n- `dispatch_task` with `mode: one-"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"shot | continuable`. Continuable children are durable across DSH restarts (SQLite-backed).\n- `dispat"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"ch_followup` / `dispatch_interrupt` / `dispatch_list` / `dispatch_get` / `get_dispatch`.\n- `dispatch"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"_probe` — zero-cost tool-name validation against `ctx.tools.view().restrictableNames` so Hermes does"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"n't burn an LLM turn on a typo.\n- `dispatch_subscribe` (v0.3.0) — discovery helper that returns the "},{"id":"p9s6","text":"SSE URL.\n- **`get_dispatch`** — read `audit.jsonl` for the most recent entries.\n- **`GET /mcp/collab"},{"id":"p9s7","text":"/stream` (v0.3.0 F1)** — `text/event-stream` of real-time events for a continuable task (lifecycle /"},{"id":"p9s8","text":" step / token / amend / followup / interrupt). Bearer-auth, `?task_id=...&since_seq=N&timeout_ms=N`."},{"id":"p9s9","text":"\n- **`GET /mcp/collab/session-stream` (v0.5.0)** — SSE feed of newly mirrored DSH session events for"},{"id":"p9s10","text":" an enabled session (`?session_id=<sid>`, `since_seq` / `timeout_ms` supported).\n- **`GET /mcp/colla"},{"id":"p9s11","text":"b/session-mirror/status` (v0.5.0)** — mirror status for one session (`?session_id=<sid>`) or all ena"},{"id":"p9s12","text":"bled sessions.\n- **Bearer auth** via `HERMES_LINK_TOKEN` env (open by default).\n- **H4 amend nonce**"},{"id":"p9s13","text":" (v0.2.2+): amend files must be named `<ts>-<task_id>-<nonce>.json`; nonce returned in `dispatch_tas"},{"id":"p9s14","text":"k` metadata.\n- **Consult reply_secret** (v0.2.2+): reply files must be named `<ticket>-<secret>.json"},{"id":"p9s15","text":"`; secret returned in the consult payload.\n- **Persona envelope**: SOUL injected (v0.2.2+); `include"},{"id":"p9s16","text":"_project_memory: true` opts in cwd-scoped MEMORY; encoding rules prevent CJK mojibake; sentinel stri"},{"id":"p9s17","text":"ngs are never paraphrased.\n- **Real measured tokens**: `ctx.tokenMeter.measure(run.localAgent)` popu"},{"id":"p9s18","text":"lates `tokens_used` on the dispatched result — no more `null` in dispatch-result."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"### User-view line (DSH → Hermes)"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| Tool | Purpose |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| `list_hermes_sessions` | enumerate Hermes archives enriched with title/model/cwd from Hermes `stat"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"e.db` |\n| `import_hermes_session` | convert a Hermes archive to a live DSH session — **click-to-resu"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"me** |\n| `load_hermes_persona` | inject Hermes SOUL.md + config into the current session (v0.2.3: no"},{"id":"p12s4","text":" longer reads MEMORY.md) |\n| `load_hermes_project_memory` | cwd-scoped Hermes MEMORY.md loader (matc"},{"id":"p12s5","text":"hes only this project's Hermes sessions) |\n| `consult_hermes` | ask Hermes a question (file-based as"},{"id":"p12s6","text":"ync; reply must carry secret suffix since v0.2.2) |\n| `mirror_session_to_hermes` | opt-in V4 mirror "},{"id":"p12s7","text":"with secret-pattern redaction (v0.2.2; cookies / JWTs / API keys / set-cookie / session_id redacted)"},{"id":"p12s8","text":"-pattern redaction (v0.2.2; cookies / JWTs / API keys / set-cookie / session_id redacted) |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### Auto-loop"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- **Startup auto-sync** imports every Hermes session into DSH.\n- **fs-watcher** polls `Hermes Home/s"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"essions/` and re-syncs on new dumps.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### Security boundaries"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"| Risk | Mitigation | Since |"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"| Cross-project context pollution (Hermes injects project-A dialogue into DSH's project-B session) |"},{"id":"p17s2","text":" main-session auto-injection disabled; MEMORY.md not broadcast; project-memory only matches cwd | v0"},{"id":"p17s3","text":".2.1 + v0.2.2 + v0.2.3 |\n| Adversary writes `amend/*` to hijack a running sub-agent | nonce-bound fi"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"lename (`<ts>-<task_id>-<nonce>.json`) | v0.2.2 |\n| Adversary writes `consult-reply/*` to impersonat"},{"id":"p17s5","text":"e Hermes | secret-bound filename (`<ticket>-<secret>.json`) | v0.2.2 |\n| Dispatched sub-agent inheri"},{"id":"p17s6","text":"ts global MEMORY notes from unrelated projects | foundation = SOUL-only; `include_project_memory: tr"},{"id":"p17s7","text":"ue` is explicit opt-in per dispatch | v0.2.2 |\n| Hermes state.db poisoned cwd → `C:\\Windows\\System32"},{"id":"p17s8","text":"` | `isSafeCwd()` rejects 17 system roots + null byte + >1024 chars | v0.2.3 |\n| Mirror filename >20"},{"id":"p17s9","text":"0 chars triggers `ENAMETOOLONG` silent failure | sha1(12 hex) tail truncation with preserved uniquen"},{"id":"p17s10","text":"ess | v0.2.3 |\n| Mirror leaks cookie / set-cookie / session_id | redact regex list expanded to 10+ s"},{"id":"p17s11","text":"ecret shapes | v0.2.3 |\n| DSH session of project A mirrored into project B's Hermes inbox | mirror p"},{"id":"p17s12","text":"olicy defaults to `scoped`: auto-enable requires a provable cwd / git-repo-root match against Hermes"},{"id":"p17s13","text":" `state.db`; an invalid policy value falls back to `scoped`, never `all` | v0.6.0 |\n| Hermes-importe"},{"id":"p17s14","text":"d session mirrored back into Hermes (transcript echo) | echo/noise guard: `hermes-*` ids and the `he"},{"id":"p17s15","text":"rmes-imported` agentPreset are never auto-enabled and never written, even when explicitly enabled; l"},{"id":"p17s16","text":"ifecycle/bookkeeping event types are skipped | v0.6.0 |\n| Imported sessions resume-unusable (`turn:0"},{"id":"p17s17","text":"` events fail DSH persistence validator) | turn envelope rewritten to start at 1; corrupt artifacts "},{"id":"p17s18","text":"auto-removed and rebuilt | v0.2.4 |"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"See docs/security-model.md for the full layered model."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"See docs/ for component-level details."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Security model"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"docs/security-model.md walks through each layer in detail. TL;DR — every cross-project channel is ex"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"plicit opt-in; every cross-process channel is authenticated; no `null` tokens, no unbounded system p"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"aths, no unredacted cookie/secret leakage."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Report vulnerabilities privately via **GitHub Security Advisories** on this repo. See SECURITY.md."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
